hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"221","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us to bring out the young girls, the veiled girls, and the menstruating women on the days of Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha to the Eid ground. As for the menstruating women, they should stay away from the prayer place and participate in the supplications of the Muslims."
"222","Hisham narrated with this chain in a similar manner."
"223","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us to bring out the veiled young girls and menstruating women on the days of Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha (to the Eid ground), so that they may participate in the prayers and supplications of the Muslims, while the menstruating women should stay away from the prayer itself."
"224","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us to bring out the young girls, menstruating women, and veiled girls to the place of Eid prayer on the two Eids. As for the menstruating women, they should stay away from the prayer area but participate in the supplications of the Muslims."
"225","Sayyidah Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! If one of us does not have a shawl?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Her sister should let her wear a part of her own shawl."
"226","Hisham narrated with this chain a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"227","The sister of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawaha (Umrah bint Rawaha, may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""It is obligatory for every woman who fastens a waistband to go (to the Eid prayer ground) on the two Eids."
"228","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led the Eid prayers, then delivered the sermon. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) also led the prayer in the same manner and then delivered the sermon. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) also led the prayer in the same manner, then delivered the sermon, and Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) also led the prayer in the same manner, then delivered the sermon. There was neither Adhan nor Iqamah in it. Mu’ammal narrated: We will say that all these noble companions led the Eid prayers without Adhan or Iqamah."
"229","It is narrated from Amr bin Dinar that he heard Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reciting the takbeers (Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar) on the days of Eid. Amr (bin Dinar) said: I do not know which of the two matters he intended. The statement of Allah Almighty: ""When you have completed the rites of Hajj, then remember Allah."" Or His statement: ""And remember Allah during the appointed number of days."
"230","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went (towards the Eid ground) on the day of Eid, then he led the prayer, then delivered the sermon, and he thought that the women had not heard it. So after three (days), he went to them, admonished and advised them, and encouraged them to give charity. So the women began to take off their earrings and rings and throw them, and Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) began to collect them in his garment."
